# {{ project_name }}

A Python service generated from `template-python-gcp-service`.

## First-time setup

```sh
./scripts/bootstrap.sh
```

`bootstrap.sh` installs uv (if missing), pins Python {{ python_version }}, installs all dependencies, installs pre-commit hooks{% if use_gcp %}, and verifies gcloud authentication against `{{ gcp_project_dev }}`{% endif %}. Re-run any time to verify environment state.

## Initializing your GitHub repository

Run these steps once after generation to set up Git Flow and push to GitHub:

```sh
# 1. Make the initial commit on develop
git add .
git commit -m "chore: initial commit"

# 2. Create main from develop
git checkout -b main
git checkout develop

# 3. Push both branches
git remote add origin <your-github-repo-url>
git push -u origin develop main
```

Then in **GitHub → repository settings**:

- **Branches → Add branch ruleset** for both `main` and `develop`:
  - Require a pull request before merging
  - Require the `CI` status check to pass
  - Require branches to be up to date before merging
- **Environments** — see [GitHub repository setup](#github-repository-setup) below.

## Day-to-day commands

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `make new-app NAME=<name>` | Scaffolds a new app under `apps/<name>/` |
| `make test` | Runs `pytest` across the workspace |
| `make lint` | Runs `ruff check` |
| `make typecheck` | Runs `pyright` in strict mode |
| `make fix` | Applies `ruff` autofixes and formats |
| `make ci` | Runs lint + typecheck + test (matches CI exactly) |
{%- if include_docker %}
| `make build NAME=<name>` | Builds the Docker image for `apps/<name>` |
{%- endif %}
{%- if use_gcp %}
| `make deploy NAME=<name> ENV=<dev\|prod>` | Deploys `apps/<name>` to the given environment |
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_terraform %}
| `make tf-plan ENV=<dev\|prod>` | Runs `terraform plan` for the given environment |
| `make tf-apply ENV=<dev\|prod>` | Runs `terraform apply` for the given environment |
{%- endif %}

